     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello,<div><br></div><div>I was wondering whether it&#39;s possible to include latent traits in the lr.fixed formula with mixedmirt(). Specifically, I&#39;m interested in estimating the correlation between F1 and F2. For example:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">mod </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> mirt</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">model</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&#39;F1 = 1-23<br>                  F2 = 24-32&#39;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br><br>mirt1 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> mixedmirt</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">data</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">dat</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> covdata </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> covdata</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> lr</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">fixed</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> list</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">F1 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><font color=\"#666600\"><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">~</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span></font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">F2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">),</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> lr</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">random </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">~</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">|</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">id</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> model </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> mod</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> itemtype</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;graded&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>Or would the COV option in the mirt.model() statement be what I need? Something like:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">mod </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> mirt</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">model</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&#39;F1 = 1-23<br>                  F2 = 24-32<br>                  COV = F1*F2)<br></span></div></code></div><br>Further, how could I see how the correlation between factors differs across groups? Thanks in advance!</div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div>"
